2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“nephrectomy” means the surgical removal of a kidney;
“patient” means a person to whom a notification referred to in regulation 3 relates;
“recipient” means the person into whose body a patient’s kidney is or will be transplanted;
“single kidney — post nephrectomy (donor)” refers to the absence of a kidney in a person due to having undergone nephrectomy for the purpose of transplantation of his kidney into the body of another living person.

3. For the purposes of section 6(1) of the Act, a notification by the manager of a healthcare institution to the Registrar that a person has undergone nephrectomy for the purpose of transplantation into the body of another living person or is undergoing any treatment for single kidney — post nephrectomy (donor), at the healthcare institution shall —
(a)contain, in relation to that patient, the information specified in the First Schedule;
(b)be made in any of the Forms set out in the Second Schedule or at the Registry’s Internet website at http://www.nrdo.gov.sg;
(c)be sent to the Registrar —
(i)by hand (including by courier);
(ii)by registered mail; or
(iii)by using such secure electronic notification system as may be approved by the Registrar; and
(d)be made within the following time:
(i)where the patient has undergone nephrectomy, not later than 3 months after the nephrectomy; or
(ii)where the patient is undergoing treatment for single kidney — post nephrectomy (donor) in the healthcare institution, not later than 3 months after the first of such treatments received by the patient at that healthcare institution on or after 1st November 2009.

THIRD SCHEDULE
Regulation 4
Additional Information for New Cases
1. Particulars of patient for new case registration:
(a)citizenship or resident status;
(b)gender;
(c)ethnic group;
(d)marital status;
(e)country of birth;
(f)educational level;
(g)employment status;
(h)relationship to recipient.
2. Particulars of recipient:
(a)name;
(b)identification number (including NRIC number, passport number, Foreign Identification Number or hospital registration number);
(c)citizenship or resident status;
(d)date of birth or age (if date of birth is unknown);
(e)gender;
(f)ethnic group;
(g)marital status;
(h)name of recipient’s healthcare institution.
3. Patient baseline information (pre-donation):
(a)date of baseline information;
(b)blood pressure;
(c)weight;
(d)height;
(e)smoking status;
(f)EQ-5D (including mobility, self-care, usual activities, pain or discomfort and anxiety or depression);
(g)diabetes mellitus;
(h)oral glucose tolerance test;
(i)hyperlipidemia;
(j)serum creatinine;
(k)creatinine clearance or radionuclide GFR;
(l)urine FEME;
(m)24-hour urine protein;
(n)whether patient is on anti-hypertensives;
(o)whether patient is on hypolipidemics;
(p)other abnormalities of kidney (including stone, cyst and others).
4. Data related to donor nephrectomy:
(a)place of surgery;
(b)name of lead surgeon;
(c)type of nephrectomy;
(d)date of initial discharge;
(e)live donor discharge disposition;
(f)complications during hospitalisation (including type(s); if the donor has renal failure or impairment, serum creatinine and whether creatinine is measured with IDMS Standard).
5. Details of notifying healthcare institution:
person who made the notification.

FOURTH SCHEDULE
Regulation 4
Additional Information for Cases
Undergoing Treatment
1. Particulars of patient (at follow-up):
(a)date of consultation;
(b)healthcare institution (including specific centre, department or clinic) responsible for subsequent treatment or follow-up;
(c)complications within 6 weeks of discharge (including type(s); if the patient has renal failure or impairment, serum creatinine and whether creatinine is measured with IDMS Standard; and if the patient has other re-hospitalisation, reason and duration);
(d)blood pressure;
(e)weight;
(f)smoking status;
(g)employment status;
(h)EQ-5D (including mobility, self-care, usual activities, pain or discomfort and anxiety or depression).
2. Risk factors (at follow-up):
(a)diabetes mellitus (including HbA1C and type of treatment if patient has diabetes mellitus; and whether the patient has impaired fasting glycemia or impaired glucose tolerance if not diabetic);
(b)hyperlipidemia.
3. Investigations (at follow-up):
(a)fasting blood sugar;
(b)serum creatinine;
(c)creatinine clearance or radionuclide GFR;
(d)Urine FEME;
(e)24-hour urine protein or urine protein or creatinine ratio.
4. Medications (at follow-up):
(a)whether patient is on anti-hypertensives;
(b)whether patient is on hypolipidemics.
5. Complications (at follow-up):
(a)other illnesses since last visit (including diagnosis);
(b)admissions to hospital since last visit (including reason and date of admission);
(c)whether or not the patient has Chronic Kidney Disease Stage 5 (including date, cause of Chronic Kidney Disease Stage 5, on transplant waiting list and reason for not on transplant waiting list).
6. Vital status:
(a)whether patient is living or deceased;
(b)where the patient is deceased, the date, place and cause of death.
7. Details of notifying healthcare institution:
person who made the notification.
